The summary of it is
Here are some basics of soldering: [1]  

Solder 

A fusible metal alloy that creates electrical connections between metal surfaces 

Clean surface 

Before soldering, make sure the surface is clean and free of oil, paint, or wax. You can use steel wool, fine sandpaper, or a solvent to clean the surface.

Soldering iron 

Heat the connection with the tip of the soldering iron for a few seconds, then apply the solder. Hold the soldering iron like a pen, near the base of the handle.  

Flux 

A chemical compound that removes oxides from the metal surfaces to help the solder bond. Flux can be corrosive to metals, so clean it off with isopropyl alcohol after soldering.

Desoldering 

If you make a mistake while soldering, you can desolder to fix it. You can apply more solder to create a stronger connection, or suck up excess solder.

Soldering station 

A soldering station holds the soldering iron and keeps solder, flux, and a sponge organized. The sponge removes oxidation from the soldering iron tip.

Fume extractor 

A fume extractor removes toxic fumes, so turn it on before soldering.

Soldering stand 

A soldering stand holds the soldering iron and provides a place to clean the tip. Some soldering irons come with their own holders.

